 Purdue University Parking Overview
Purdue University offers various parking services and information for students, faculty, and visitors. Key sections include permits, carpool options, green benefits, maps and regulations, parking citations, FAQs, and contact information. The university emphasizes sustainable transportation options and provides resources for low emission vehicles.


__________________________________________________
 Low Emission Vehicle Parking
Individuals driving a low emission vehicle (LEV) can park in designated spaces with a valid "A" permit. The American Council for an Energy-Efficient Economy (ACEEE) maintains a list of qualifying vehicles starting from 1998 models. Purdue has four LEV spaces located in the Northwestern Avenue Parking Garage at 504 Northwestern Avenue, West Lafayette, IN. These spaces are situated on Level F Black, ground level, on the north side.


__________________________________________________
 LEV Parking Locations
- **Location**: Northwestern Avenue Parking Garage
- **Address**: 504 Northwestern Avenue, West Lafayette, IN
- **LEV Spaces**: Four spaces available on Level F Black, ground level, north side.


