WEBPAGE: www.purdue.edu_parking_green_benefits_campus-transit.htm

 Purdue University Parking Overview
Purdue University Parking provides essential information regarding parking permits, carpooling options, green benefits, maps and regulations, parking citations, and FAQs. The university has partnered with SP Plus (SP+) to enhance on-campus transit services starting August 14, 2025, for the 2025-26 academic year. This section serves as a hub for all parking-related information at Purdue University.


__________________________________________________
 Campus Transit Services
Purdue University has expanded its campus transit services in collaboration with SP Plus (SP+), effective from August 14, 2025. The transit services will operate throughout the academic year when classes are in session. Key features include:

- **Mobile App**: The Purdue Campus Transit app is free for students, faculty, and staff, available on both the Apple App Store and Google Play Store. Users can track vehicles in real-time, schedule rides, and view fixed transit routes.
- **Fixed Routes**: Three primary routes will operate Monday through Friday from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.:
  1. **Ross-Ade Loop**: Covers various streets including Cherry Lane and Northwestern Avenue.
  2. **Purdue Mall Loop**: Includes Stadium Avenue and N. Martin Jischke Drive.
  3. **Discovery Park Loop**: Follows Mitch Daniels Boulevard and Memorial Mall Drive.
  
- **On-Demand Service**: Available Monday through Friday from 7 a.m. to 12 a.m., with designated pick-up and drop-off locations. Evening-only routes are available from 7 p.m. to 12 a.m. on weekdays, and Sunday service runs from 4 p.m. to 9 p.m.


__________________________________________________
 App Instructions and Features
The Purdue Campus Transit mobile app allows users to:
- Download and set up an account.
- Track rides, plan trips, and receive notifications.
- Request on-demand rides and track drivers in real-time.


__________________________________________________
 Safety Measures
Purdue Campus Transit has implemented various safety measures to ensure the well-being of its riders. Specific details about these measures can be found on the Purdue Campus Transit website.


__________________________________________________
 Green Benefits and Sustainable Transportation
Purdue University promotes green benefits through various transportation options, including:
- **CityBus**: Local public transportation.
- **Electric Vehicle Charging Stations**: Facilities for electric vehicle users.
- **Low Emission Vehicles**: Encouragement of environmentally friendly transportation.
- **Veo Bicycles and Scooters**: Shared mobility options for students and staff.
- **Zipcars**: Car-sharing services available on campus.


__________________________________________________
 Contact Information
For further inquiries or issues related to parking, users can contact Purdue University Parking at parking@purdue.edu or call (765) 494-4600. The university is located at 610 Purdue Mall, West Lafayette, IN 47907.


__________________________________________________

