final expanded context: WEBPAGE: parking.indianapolis.iu.edu_transportation_bus_indygo.html

IndyGo Bus Services Overview
IndyGo bus services provide an effective transit option for students and employees at Indiana University Indianapolis to travel to campus and navigate the city. The Parking & Transportation office sells IndyGo bus passes, including a discounted option for students.
__________________________________________________
IndyGo Pass Types and Pricing
The following IndyGo pass types and their prices are available for purchase:
- **IndyGo 31-Day S-Pass**: $30 (available to students only; limited to one purchase per month)
- **IndyGo 31-Day Pass**: $60 (available to anyone)
- **IndyGo 7-Day Pass**: $15.75 (available to anyone)
- **IndyGo Half-Fare 31-Day Pass**: $30 (available only to individuals with an IndyGo Half-Fare ID Card)

Note: Lost or stolen passes will not be replaced, and all sales are final with no returns or exchanges.
__________________________________________________
IndyGo Bus Stops and Routes
IndyGo buses stop at various locations, including:
- Indiana Avenue (Route 6-Harding)
- Michigan Street (Routes 3-Michigan St., 10-10th St., and 37-Park 100)

Additionally, the IU Indianapolis JAGLINE shuttle system connects to IndyGo's Red Line station at Capital Ave. and Vermont St. (Route 5-Purple).
__________________________________________________
Additional Information and Resources
For more information regarding IndyGo passes, visit [IndyGo Fares and Passes](http://www.indygo.net/fares-and-passes/).
__________________________________________________
Context
__________________________________________________

WEBPAGE: www.purdue.edu_vpec_ocr_accessibility-resources_access-guide_parking-transportation-access_

Parking & Transportation Access
Accessible parking is available for students, staff, and visitors at Purdue University. Requests for accessible parking will be prioritized for those who can demonstrate a condition or impairment that significantly limits mobility. Visitors can utilize metered disability spaces (marked with blue and white handicap signs) by displaying the appropriate license plate or official handicap placard on their vehicle dashboard. For the locations of metered disability spaces, refer to the Campus Parking Map, where you can enable the ADA Parking layer to view accessible parking areas.

Accessible parking spaces are available in all parking garages, including:
- Grant Street Parking Garage, 120 N. Grant Street
- Harrison Street Parking Garage, 719 Clinic Drive

Visitors needing to use spaces that require an “A” permit along with a disability license plate or official placard can purchase a daily permit for $5 through the online parking portal.

To report any barriers in parking lots and garages (e.g., broken elevators, icy access aisles), contact Parking Facilities at (765) 494-9494 or via email at parking@purdue.edu.
__________________________________________________
City Bus Services
ACCESS, the CityBus Paratransit Service, operates during the same hours and to the same destinations as regular route buses. It offers "curb to curb" service for individuals who qualify and complete the application process, covering locations within ¾ mile of a regular route. For inquiries, contact CityBus ACCESS at 765-742-2121 or visit them at CityBus ACCESS, 1250 Canal Road, Lafayette, IN 47904. Applications for ACCESS can be found on the CityBus website.
__________________________________________________
Purdue Campus Transit
Purdue Campus Transit operates a fleet of vehicles, including Ford E-Transit vans and transit buses, all designed to comply with ADA standards. These vehicles are equipped with wheelchair lifts or ramps, secure tie-down systems, accessible seating, and advanced safety features. Each stop is announced for passenger convenience.

The On-Demand service features ADA accessible vans and can be requested via the Campus Transit mobile app. This service is available at designated pick-up and drop-off locations from Monday to Friday, 7 a.m. to 12 a.m., with additional routes available in the evening.
__________________________________________________
Communication and Resources
The website provides various communication tools and resources for the Purdue community, including:
- OneCampus Portal
