Final Answer:
To set up CityBus for off-campus transit at Purdue University, you need to follow these steps:  1.
**Obtain an Off-Campus Pass**: For the fall 2025 semester, Purdue is subsidizing the cost of off-
campus bus passes. The original price is $99, but with the subsidy, you will only pay $25 for the
semester. You can find details about purchasing the pass on the CityBus website.  2. **Use a Valid
Purdue ID**: Ensure you have a valid Purdue ID to access discounts for both on-campus and off-campus
CityBus services.  3. **Plan Your Routes**: Visit the CityBus website to review the routes that
connect to your desired destinations. Utilize the trip planner tools available on the site to find
the best routes based on your starting point and destination.  4. **Download the CityBus App**: This
app will help you track buses in real-time, check schedules, and receive alerts about service
changes.  5. **Familiarize Yourself with Bus Stops**: Identify the nearest bus stop to your location
and study the schedule for your specific route.  6. **Stay Updated**: Follow any updates from the
CityBus regarding route changes or detours. This information is usually available through their app
or website.  For further assistance, you can contact CityBus or Purdue's transportation services if
you have specific questions regarding the process.
