final expanded context: WEBPAGE: parking.indianapolis.iu.edu_transportation_bus_indygo.html

IndyGo Bus Services Overview
IndyGo bus services provide an effective transit option for students and employees at Indiana University Indianapolis to travel to campus and navigate the city. The Parking & Transportation office sells IndyGo bus passes, including a discounted option for students.
__________________________________________________
IndyGo Pass Types and Pricing
The following IndyGo pass types and their prices are available for purchase:
- **IndyGo 31-Day S-Pass**: $30 (available to students only; limited to one purchase per month)
- **IndyGo 31-Day Pass**: $60 (available to anyone)
- **IndyGo 7-Day Pass**: $15.75 (available to anyone)
- **IndyGo Half-Fare 31-Day Pass**: $30 (available only to individuals with an IndyGo Half-Fare ID Card)

Note: Lost or stolen passes will not be replaced, and all sales are final with no returns or exchanges.
__________________________________________________
IndyGo Bus Stops and Routes
IndyGo buses stop at various locations, including:
- Indiana Avenue (Route 6-Harding)
- Michigan Street (Routes 3-Michigan St., 10-10th St., and 37-Park 100)

Additionally, the IU Indianapolis JAGLINE shuttle system connects to IndyGo's Red Line station at Capital Ave. and Vermont St. (Route 5-Purple).
__________________________________________________
Additional Information and Resources
For more information regarding IndyGo passes, visit [IndyGo Fares and Passes](http://www.indygo.net/fares-and-passes/).
__________________________________________________
Context
__________________________________________________

WEBPAGE: www.purdue.edu_parking_green_benefits_campus-transit-faqs.html

 Purdue University Campus Transit - Overview
Purdue University has partnered with SP Plus (SP+) to enhance on-campus transit services, branded as Purdue Campus Transit, starting in the 2025-26 academic year. This initiative aims to improve the transit experience for the campus community through technology adoption and operational enhancements.


__________________________________________________
 Bicycle Loading Instructions
13. **Bicycle Policy**: Bikes can be brought on Campus Transit vehicles. Instructional videos and a Bike Loading Guide are available to assist riders in loading their bikes properly.


__________________________________________________

__________________________________________________
 Context
This chunk serves as an informative guide about the upcoming changes to transit services at Purdue University, highlighting the transition to a new provider and the benefits for students and staff. It is essential for those interested in campus transportation options and policies.
__________________________________________________
 RFP for Campus Transit
1. **Purpose of RFP**: The Request for Proposals (RFP) was issued to enhance the transit experience for the campus community by inviting vendors to propose innovative solutions that meet campus needs.
2. **Evaluation Process**: Eight proposals were received, including one from CityBus. An evaluation team comprising representatives from various university departments selected SP+ as the preferred vendor, which has a three-year contract with options for two one-year renewals.


__________________________________________________
 About SP+
3. **Company Background**: SP+ is a subsidiary of Metropolis, an AI company specializing in checkout-free payment experiences. Metropolis has become the largest parking network in North America, managing over 4,000 locations.


__________________________________________________
 Service Details
4. **Start Date**: Purdue Campus Transit will commence on August 14, 2025.
5. **Eligibility and Fees**: All individuals with a valid Purdue ID, including students, faculty, staff, and retirees from Purdue West Lafayette and Indianapolis, can ride the shuttles for free.
6. **Routes and Schedules**: The routes and schedules for Purdue Campus Transit will be available online, differing from those previously operated by CityBus.


__________________________________________________
 Off-Campus Transit
7. **CityBus Service**: CityBus will continue to provide off-campus transit services, with Purdue subsidizing the cost of off-campus student passes for the fall 2025 semester. Details about these passes can be found online.


__________________________________________________
 CityBus Route Changes
8. **Route Management**: Changes to CityBus routes servicing the Purdue/West Lafayette area will be at CityBus's discretion, as Purdue does not control these non-campus loops.


__________________________________________________
 Summer Service
9. **CityBus Availability**: Information regarding CityBus service during the summer can be found on the CityBus website.


__________________________________________________
 Shuttle Features
10. **Shuttle Compliance**: Purdue Campus Transit shuttles will comply with ADA requirements and include bicycle racks.
11. **Fleet Composition**: The fleet will consist of low-floor transit buses, midsized shuttles, and electric transit vans.


__________________________________________________
 Transit App
12. **Mobile Application**: The Purdue Campus Transit app is available for download on both the Apple App Store and Google Play Store, allowing users to view routes, track vehicles in real-time, and schedule on-demand rides.


__________________________________________________

